# Product Requirements (PRD)

Write PRDs to `docs/prd/<feature>.md` using this template:

```markdown
# <Feature Name>

## Problem
What user pain or business need does this solve?

## Users
Who benefits? Primary and secondary personas.

## User Stories
| ID | Story | Priority | Acceptance Criteria |
|----|-------|----------|---------------------|
| US-1 | As a … I want … so that … | P0/P1/P2 | Given/When/Then |

## Non-Goals
Explicitly out of scope for this iteration.

## Success Metrics
Measurable outcomes (adoption, latency, error rate, etc.).

## Open Questions
Decisions needed before architecture.
```

## Guidelines

- Acceptance criteria must be testable (Given/When/Then).
- P0 = MVP blocker; P1 = important; P2 = nice-to-have.
- Keep PRDs outcome-focused, not implementation-prescriptive.
- Hand off to `architect` with open technical questions listed.
